    "content": "<div style=\"display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem\"><span style=\"background:#dc2626;color:white;padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:.3rem;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600\">Binding</span> <span class=\"tag\">EU</span></div> <h1>CSOAI Charter × DORA</h1> <p class=\"lead\">Binding ICT resilience regulation for the EU financial sector. Requires ICT risk management, incident reporting, resilience testing and third-party risk oversight. AI systems used in financial services fall in scope.</p> <div class=\"meta-bar\"> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Cite:</strong> Regulation (EU) 2022/2554</span> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Effective:</strong> 17 January 2025</span> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Free until:</strong> 2 December 2027 (free tier for in-scope financial entities)</span> </div> <div class=\"alert\"> <strong>⚠ Deadline:</strong> DORA has been in effect since **17 January 2025**. The 4-hour major-incident reporting clock is one of the tightest in EU law. Financial firms using AI need both DORA and EU AI Act coverage by Aug 2028. </div> <h2>Crosswalk: clause-by-clause</h2> <p>Each row maps a DORA clause to the relevant CSOAI Charter article(s) and the MCP(s) that operationalise it.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th style=\"width:38%\">DORA Clause</th> <th style=\"width:34%\">CSOAI Charter Article(s)</th> <th style=\"width:28%\">MCP(s)</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Article 5 — ICT Risk Management Framework</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 2 (Provable Safety), Article 13 (Risk Management)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-dora, csoai-dora-rms</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Article 9 — ICT Risk Management Tools</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 19 (Robustness), Article 36 (Logging)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-dora</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Article 17 — ICT-Related Incident Management</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 39 (Incident Response)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-ai-incident-reporting</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Article 19 — Major ICT-Related Incident Reporting (4-hour clock)</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 39 (Incident Response, 4h Critical)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-dora, csoai-ai-incident-reporting</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Article 24 — Digital Operational Resilience Testing</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 21 (Continuous Verification)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-mcp-test</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Article 28 — Third-Party Risk</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 23 (Supply Chain Risk)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-dora-nis2-crosswalk</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2>How to use this crosswalk</h2> <ol> <li><strong>Compliance teams</strong> — import this crosswalk as the DORA ↔ ISMS mapping for your audit dossier.</li> <li><strong>Procurement teams</strong> — paste the relevant rows into your RFP responses to demonstrate framework coverage.</li> <li><strong>Developers</strong> — `pip install` the named MCPs to add runtime enforcement to your AI pipeline.</li> <li><strong>Researchers</strong> — cite freely under CC BY 4.0.</li> </ol> <h2>Cite this crosswalk</h2> <pre class=\"cite-block\">CSOAI Charter × DORA Crosswalk v1.0. CSOAI LTD (UK Companies House 16939677). https://csoai.org/frameworks/dora. CC BY 4.0. Accessed [date].</pre> <div class=\"cta\"> <h2>Get measured before 2 December 2027 (free tier for in-scope financial entities)</h2> <p style=\"color:#e6f7ec;margin:.5rem 0\">Free CSOAI measurement covers all 22+ frameworks including DORA.</p> <a href=\"/start\">Get Measured →</a> See AI Self-State Index <a href=\"/framework-catalog\">All 22+ Frameworks</a> </div> <p class=\"foot\">© 2026 CSOAI LTD · UK Companies House <strong>16939677</strong><br> Crosswalk · CC BY 4.0 · <a href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a> · <a href=\"mailto:nicholas@csoai.org\">Contact</a><br> <em>\"Open methodology. Independently verifiable.\"</em></p>",
