    "content": "<div style=\"display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem\"><span style=\"background:#d97706;color:white;padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:.3rem;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600\">Voluntary</span> <span class=\"tag\">United States (federal voluntary)</span></div> <h1>CSOAI Charter × NIST AI RMF 1.0</h1> <p class=\"lead\">Voluntary US framework with four functions: Govern, Map, Measure, Manage. The GenAI Profile (NIST AI 600-1, July 2024) extends to large generative models. Increasingly cited in US executive orders, federal procurement and state laws.</p> <div class=\"meta-bar\"> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Cite:</strong> NIST AI 100-1</span> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Effective:</strong> January 2023 (1.0) · GenAI Profile July 2024</span> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Free until:</strong> 2 December 2027</span> </div> <div class=\"alert\"> <strong>⚠ Deadline:</strong> Voluntary but increasingly mandatory: California AB-2013, Colorado AI Act (1 Feb 2026) and federal AI executive orders all cite NIST AI RMF. </div> <h2>Crosswalk: clause-by-clause</h2> <p>Each row maps a NIST AI RMF 1.0 clause to the relevant CSOAI Charter article(s) and the MCP(s) that operationalise it.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th style=\"width:38%\">NIST AI RMF 1.0 Clause</th> <th style=\"width:34%\">CSOAI Charter Article(s)</th> <th style=\"width:28%\">MCP(s)</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Govern — Function 1 (5 categories, 19 subcategories)</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Articles 9, 11 (Governance)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-nist-ai-rmf</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Map — Function 2 (5 categories, 18 subcategories)</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 14 (Impact Assessment)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-iso-42005, csoai-nist-ai-rmf</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Measure — Function 3 (4 categories, 19 subcategories)</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 21 (Continuous Verification)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-mcp-test, csoai-bias-detection</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Manage — Function 4 (4 categories, 16 subcategories)</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Articles 16-25 (Operational)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-nist-ai-rmf</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>GenAI Profile (AI 600-1) — 12 categories</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Articles 18 (Provenance), 24 (Bias), 41 (GenAI)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-watermark-attest, csoai-bias-detection</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2>How to use this crosswalk</h2> <ol> <li><strong>Compliance teams</strong> — import this crosswalk as the NIST AI RMF 1.0 ↔ ISMS mapping for your audit dossier.</li> <li><strong>Procurement teams</strong> — paste the relevant rows into your RFP responses to demonstrate framework coverage.</li> <li><strong>Developers</strong> — `pip install` the named MCPs to add runtime enforcement to your AI pipeline.</li> <li><strong>Researchers</strong> — cite freely under CC BY 4.0.</li> </ol> <h2>Cite this crosswalk</h2> <pre class=\"cite-block\">CSOAI Charter × NIST AI RMF 1.0 Crosswalk v1.0. CSOAI LTD (UK Companies House 16939677). https://csoai.org/frameworks/nist-ai-rmf. CC BY 4.0. Accessed [date].</pre> <div class=\"cta\"> <h2>Get measured before 2 December 2027</h2> <p style=\"color:#e6f7ec;margin:.5rem 0\">Free CSOAI measurement covers all 22+ frameworks including NIST AI RMF 1.0.</p> <a href=\"/start\">Get Measured →</a> See AI Self-State Index <a href=\"/framework-catalog\">All 22+ Frameworks</a> </div> <p class=\"foot\">© 2026 CSOAI LTD · UK Companies House <strong>16939677</strong><br> Crosswalk · CC BY 4.0 · <a href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a> · <a href=\"mailto:nicholas@csoai.org\">Contact</a><br> <em>\"Open methodology. Independently verifiable.\"</em></p>",
