    "css": " .legacy-content :root{--ink:#0f172a;--muted:#5a5e66;--gold:#c9a84c;--card:#f7f8fa;--border:#e6e8ec;--brand:#0a8a3f;--warn:#dc2626;--accent:#fef3c7} .legacy-content *{box-sizing:border-box} .legacy-content body{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;max-width:980px;margin:2.5rem auto;padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.65} .legacy-content nav.crumbs{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.5rem} .legacy-content nav.crumbs a{color:var(--brand);text-decoration:none} .legacy-content h1{margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:2.1rem;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.2} .legacy-content h2{margin-top:2.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--brand);padding-bottom:.4rem;font-size:1.4rem} .legacy-content a{color:var(--brand);text-decoration:none} .legacy-content a:hover{text-decoration:underline} .legacy-content .lead{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.1rem;max-width:760px;margin-top:.75rem} .legacy-content .meta-bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin:1rem 0 0;align-items:center} .legacy-content .tag{background:var(--card);color:var(--muted);padding:.25rem .7rem;border-radius:.3rem;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:500;border:1px solid var(--border)} .legacy-content .alert{background:#fef3c7;border-left:4px solid #d97706;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:.35rem;color:#78350f} .legacy-content .alert strong{color:#92400e} .legacy-content table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:1rem 0;background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.45rem;overflow:hidden} .legacy-content th{background:#f0f9ff;color:var(--ink);text-align:left;padding:.8rem .5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--brand);font-weight:600;font-size:.85rem} .legacy-content td{font-size:.92rem} .legacy-content .cite-block{background:#0f172a;color:#e2e8f0;padding:.9rem 1.1rem;border-radius:.45rem;font-size:.82rem;overflow-x:auto;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace} .legacy-content .cta{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--brand) 0%,#076a30 100%);color:white;padding:1.5rem;border-radius:.55rem;margin:2rem 0;text-align:center} .legacy-content .cta h2{color:white;border:none;margin-top:0;padding-bottom:.3rem} .legacy-content .cta a{background:white;color:var(--brand);padding:.55rem 1.25rem;border-radius:.35rem;display:inline-block;margin:.3rem;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none} .legacy-content .cta a:hover{background:#f0fdf4;text-decoration:none} .legacy-content .foot{margin-top:3rem;color:#888;font-size:.85rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:1.5rem} ",
    "content": "<div style=\"display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem\"><span style=\"background:#d97706;color:white;padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:.3rem;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600\">Voluntary</span> <span class=\"tag\">OECD (50+ adopting countries)</span></div> <h1>CSOAI Charter × OECD AI Principles</h1> <p class=\"lead\">5 values-based principles + 5 recommendations for national policy. Foundational text adopted by 50+ countries. The 2024 revision added GenAI-specific guidance and synthetic content provenance.</p> <div class=\"meta-bar\"> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Cite:</strong> OECD/LEGAL/0449</span> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Effective:</strong> May 2019 · revised May 2024</span> <span class=\"tag\"><strong>Free until:</strong> 2 December 2027</span> </div> <div class=\"alert\"> <strong>⚠ Deadline:</strong> Cited by virtually every other AI framework as foundational. UK AI Bill, Canada AIDA, Korea AI Basic Act and Council of Europe AI Convention all reference OECD. </div> <h2>Crosswalk: clause-by-clause</h2> <p>Each row maps a OECD AI Principles clause to the relevant CSOAI Charter article(s) and the MCP(s) that operationalise it.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th style=\"width:38%\">OECD AI Principles Clause</th> <th style=\"width:34%\">CSOAI Charter Article(s)</th> <th style=\"width:28%\">MCP(s)</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Principle 1.1 — Inclusive growth, sustainable development</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 8 (Prosperity Covenant)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-oecd-cite</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Principle 1.2 — Human-centred values and fairness</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 1 (Maternal Covenant), Article 24 (Bias)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-bias-detection</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Principle 1.3 — Transparency and explainability</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 17 (Transparency)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-watermark-attest</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Principle 1.4 — Robustness, security and safety</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Article 2 (Provable Safety), Article 19 (Robustness)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-mcp-test</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\"><strong>Principle 1.5 — Accountability</strong></td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top\">Charter Articles 11, 39 (Accountability + Incident)</td> <td style=\"padding:.7rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #e6e8ec;vertical-align:top;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8rem;color:#0a8a3f\">csoai-ai-incident-reporting</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2>How to use this crosswalk</h2> <ol> <li><strong>Compliance teams</strong> — import this crosswalk as the OECD AI Principles ↔ ISMS mapping for your audit dossier.</li> <li><strong>Procurement teams</strong> — paste the relevant rows into your RFP responses to demonstrate framework coverage.</li> <li><strong>Developers</strong> — `pip install` the named MCPs to add runtime enforcement to your AI pipeline.</li> <li><strong>Researchers</strong> — cite freely under CC BY 4.0.</li> </ol> <h2>Cite this crosswalk</h2> <pre class=\"cite-block\">CSOAI Charter × OECD AI Principles Crosswalk v1.0. CSOAI LTD (UK Companies House 16939677). https://csoai.org/frameworks/oecd-ai-principles. CC BY 4.0. Accessed [date].</pre> <div class=\"cta\"> <h2>Get measured before 2 December 2027</h2> <p style=\"color:#e6f7ec;margin:.5rem 0\">Free CSOAI measurement covers all 22+ frameworks including OECD AI Principles.</p> <a href=\"/start\">Get Measured →</a> See AI Self-State Index <a href=\"/framework-catalog\">All 22+ Frameworks</a> </div> <p class=\"foot\">© 2026 CSOAI LTD · UK Companies House <strong>16939677</strong><br> Crosswalk · CC BY 4.0 · <a href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a> · <a href=\"mailto:nicholas@csoai.org\">Contact</a><br> <em>\"Open methodology. Independently verifiable.\"</em></p>",
